1
00:00:00,790 --> 00:00:02,510
The chairman is the leader of the board.

2
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:05,110
He is also a non-executive director.

3
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:07,610
In some cases, the chairman could be an

4
00:00:07,610 --> 00:00:09,430
independent non-executive director.

5
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:11,130
I'll speak about that in a minute.

6
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:13,430
However, the chairman is the leader of the

7
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:13,690
board.

8
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:16,470
He is also referred to as first amongst

9
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:16,950
equals.

10
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:20,230
One of the responsibilities that the chairman has

11
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:22,310
is to ensure that as much as possible,

12
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:25,530
all of the directors on the board contribute

13
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:28,990
effectively to the discussions on the board.

14
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:32,370
So to give an illustration of that, when

15
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:34,570
you have new directors on the board, there's

16
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:37,030
a tendency for them to sort of feel

17
00:00:37,030 --> 00:00:39,430
like they need to understand the dynamics of

18
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:42,630
the board and might spend time, sometimes too

19
00:00:42,630 --> 00:00:45,690
long a period, to get acclimatised and so

20
00:00:45,690 --> 00:00:46,950
they remain quiet for a while.

21
00:00:47,530 --> 00:00:49,430
The chairman's responsibility is to make them feel

22
00:00:49,430 --> 00:00:52,850
comfortable and actually seek them out and have

23
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:55,430
them contribute effectively to discussions.

24
00:00:56,270 --> 00:00:58,650
The chairman also acts as a link between

25
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:01,510
the board and management.

26
00:01:02,310 --> 00:01:06,150
He or she essentially gives guidance to the

27
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:08,150
CEO or the MD, as we had spoken

28
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:11,270
about, and ensures that whatever information the board

29
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:14,030
wants to pass to management, as much as

30
00:01:14,030 --> 00:01:16,850
possible, he acts as that link person.

31
00:01:19,140 --> 00:01:22,000
There's tenure restriction on directors, I must say,

32
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:25,460
under the different codes of corporate governance, now

33
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:26,200
guidelines.

34
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:28,880
The Nigerian Code of Corporate Governance, which is

35
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:30,520
the one that I'll be referencing a lot

36
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:33,000
in the course of this session, does not

37
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,400
specify a tenure for the categories of directors

38
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:39,180
I've spoken about, i.e. the EDs and

39
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:41,140
the non-executive directors.

40
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:45,880
The specific sectoral codes, for instance the CBN

41
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:49,980
guidelines, fixes a maximum tenure of 12 years

42
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:52,340
for these categories of directors.

43
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:55,720
The third category of directors is the independent

44
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:57,280
non-executive director.

45
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:00,620
This category of directors are expected to serve

46
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,720
on the board for not longer than 9

47
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:06,020
years in the case of non-financial institutions

48
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:08,759
and 8 years in the case of financial

49
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:09,620
institutions.

50
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:14,280
Essentially, they bring a level of independence, not

51
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:16,960
just in the way they are appointed, which

52
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:22,000
is critical, but also in their own situations

53
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:22,580
as well.

54
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,400
So they're not expected to be representatives of

55
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:26,340
significant shareholders.

56
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:30,120
In fact, typically they're not expected to hold

57
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,480
shares in the company.

58
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,800
The Nigerian Code of Corporate Governance specifies a

59
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,820
minimum number of shares they can hold, which

60
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:39,060
is 0.01%, very minimal.

61
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:42,820
But best practise would stipulate that they shouldn't

62
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:45,380
even own shares in the business because they

63
00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:48,420
bring independent judgments and they're not expected to

64
00:02:48,420 --> 00:02:50,740
be that involved in the business.

65
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:53,260
The only connection they have with the business

66
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:54,520
is their directorship.

67
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:58,640
They also shouldn't have been regulators in the

68
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,440
last 5 years, they shouldn't have been employed

69
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:03,480
by the company in any capacity, either as

70
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:05,360
employees or as consultants.

71
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:08,180
The whole essence of having independent directors on

72
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:11,460
the board is to have a situation where

73
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:14,840
you don't have too much power residing in

74
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:18,680
either the executives or the shareholder representatives, i

75
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:20,340
.e. the non-executive directors.

76
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:25,060
Independent directors are critical to the composition of

77
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:27,760
the board because they bring independent judgement.

78
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,780
And that kind of conversation is important when

79
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:34,880
we're discussing things like remuneration, dividend to shareholders,

80
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:39,020
or proposals of management that seems to be

81
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:42,340
more tilted towards the requirements of management.

82
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:45,720
So they bring that balance to board discussions.

83
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:49,740
But the most critical part of the independence,

84
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:52,500
in my view, is the appointment process.

85
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,400
How are independent directors appointed?

86
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:57,360
Typically they are appointed through a rigorous process

87
00:03:57,360 --> 00:04:02,200
that entails a consultant that would use the

88
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:05,960
criteria provided by the company to determine the

89
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:07,960
kinds of people that would fit into the

90
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:11,520
profile provided by the company.

91
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:14,960
But beyond the fact of their independence, independent

92
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,420
directors are also expected to bring some level

93
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:20,279
of expertise, some level of experience, whether it's

94
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:21,900
technology, whether it's marketing.

95
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:24,660
They also bring some skills to add to

96
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:26,940
the diversity of the board.
